From 85c9e913dc177977a45eeba2bff579c94e53db32 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andre Watson <dre@ligandal.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 00:01:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 27/32] perf(moe): lossless ILP finalizeMoeRouting via private
 flashinfer build (SGLANG_QWENOPT_FUSE_MOE_FINALIZE_ILP)

The stock finalize walks top-k serially (3 dependent global loads per k, 1 CTA/token). The patched
variant gathers routing metadata once, issues all k row loads before accumulating and splits columns
over gridDim.y; per-element fp32 arithmetic and k order are unchanged. Only
cutlass_fused_moe_instantiation.cu is recompiled; other objects are reused read-only.
GPU2 proxy, real layer-20 NVFP4 experts + real routing, 124 windows T=1..16: output BITWISE equal to
stock, deterministic, CUDA-graph replay == eager. finalize 8.63 -> 4.54 us at T=4; wall -4.4 us/call.
Off by default; unset -> stock module untouched.
